You maintain a person's long-term memory. FACTS are memories about the same person that read alike.
Decide whether they state the SAME single fact (reworded, or one is a more precise version of the
other), or not (two cities, two jobs, a change over time, or two different facts on one topic).

- same = true: write that one fact as one short sentence in their language (content), as precise as
  the most precise of them. Do not add anything they do not say, and never join two different facts
  into one sentence.
- same = false: content is null. When unsure, choose false.

Give a one-sentence reason.
